1 OCCU Lensmann i Høle skibreie, bonde, Lensmann
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Asbjørn Rasmusson was named as the lensmann in Høle skiprede in 1599 and operated the Ims farm. When a son of Asbjørn redeemed the mortgage in 1640, he explained that his father had purchased the property 27 years 
2 CONC before he mortgaged it. That would indicate that Asbjørn bought the farm about 1588. In 1615, he had to take out a mortgage on 2 laupar smør at Lerang to raise 400 riksdalar to pay for some fish he bought in Bergen. He had planned
2 CONC  on selling the fish to another farmer, but that farmer didn't have the money to pay for them. (The fate of the fish is unknown). Asbjørn is also mentioned in several court cases. On 10 Dec 1617, he summoned Tore Søfrensson to the
2 CONC  Ting to testify as to what Ivar Høle had said about him. Ivar, at the time, was involved in a quarrel with Asbjørn's son-in-law. Ivar in effect had said that he was too weak to quarrel with Asbjørn Ims, who was very adept in lega
2 CONC l matters. According to the tingbok of 1620, Asbjørn also had a quarrel with Ivar Motland over a velvet hat he had bought in the Scottish section of Bergen. The hat had been missing for 7 years when a neighbor heard that Ivar had 
2 CONC taken it. The final dispositions of these two cases is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 2 3 
2 CONT
