1 OCCU Lensmann i Høle, Lensmann, Lensmann nevnt 1591, lensmann, Høle
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rasmus Halvarsson is first named as the lensmann of Høle skiprede in a document from the 1580's. In 1591, Rasmus represented Høle at the royal coronation in Oslo. He turned his farm over to his son sometime before 
2 CONC 1599. There is a considerable amount of circumstantial evidence indicating that Rasmus was descended from the so-called "Lagmannsætta of Talgje", that is Gard Toresson and Ramborg Knutsdatter. The names Rasmus and Halvar are found
2 CONC  in the UnderBerge family, which can directly trace descent from Gard Toresson. The name "Israel" shows up among Rasmus' descendants and is also a prominent name in ancestors of the "Holy Birgitte." But probably the most significa
2 CONC nt thing is that both families (Ims and UnderBerge) used bumerke with a capital latin "A" in the lower half. 
1 FAMC @F6000000014350774616@
1 FAMS @F6000000006979688512@
1 RFN geni:6000000002280842017
